'''Water Horse''' is a [[Spells|spell]] that creates a horse out of water. It is used in the [[contraption]] [[Water Horse Carriage]].

==Description==
: ''See [[Water Horse Carriage]] for a Description of the Contraption''
[[File:Water Horse Spell Redraw.png|left|120px|thumb|<small>Redraw of Water Horse Casting Seal</small>]] The Casting Seal contains a [[Sigils#Water|Sigil of Water]] in its center and a [[Sigils#Horse|Decorative Sigil of the Horse]] above it. [[Signs#Mimicry|Signs of Mimicry]] sit on either side of the [[Sigils#Water|central sigil]] while two [[Signs#Columns|Signs of Columns]] pointing in opposite directions are placed on either side of the [[Sigils#Horse|decorative sigil]]. Underneath the [[Sigils#Water|Sigil of Water]] is an alternating pattern of three unknown symbols and two [[Signs#Regions|Signs of Regions]] pointing downwards.{{Ref|m|46|10}}{{Ref|[[Archives of Witch Hat Atelier]], Page 150}}

This spell is likely to be a sculpting spell, specifically a [[watersculpture]], given its use of a [[Decorative Sigils|decorative sigil]]. The two sigils allow for the creation of water that takes the shape of a horse while the [[Signs#Mimicry|Signs of Mimicry]] guide its movements. The Water Horse can be mounted, guided and controlled by its caster, much like a regular horse.{{Ref|[[Archives of Witch Hat Atelier]], Page 150}}

==History==
: ''See [[Water Horse Carriage]] for the History of the Contraption''
While searching for [[Richeh]], [[Agott]] and [[Euini]] in the [[Serpentback Cave]], [[Qifrey]] catches sight of [[Sasaran]] and immediately pursues him by casting and mounting Water Horse using a [[Seal Scroll|seal scroll]].{{Ref|m|27|4-5}}

The Water Horse seal can be seen on the [[Water Horse Carriage]] [[contraption]]. It is located on the breastplate of the carriage's harness and allows for the conjured Water Horse to draw the carriage forward. While travelling to [[Ezrest|Ezrest City]] with [[Qifrey's Atelier|his apprentices]] for [[Silver Eve]], Qifrey controls the Water Horse's movements using a long, wooden staff with a scroll of paper hanging off the other end. After lowering the scroll to the ground and detaching it from the staff, the spell stops taking effect.{{Ref|m|46|11-13}}

